  ORGANISM  unidentified cloning vector
            other sequences; artificial sequences; vectors.
REFERENCE   1
  AUTHORS   Rose,M.D., Novick,P., Thomas,J.H., Botstein,D. and Fink,G.R.
  TITLE     A Saccharomyces cerevisiae genomic plasmid bank based on a
            centromere-containing shuttle vector
  JOURNAL   Gene 60 (2-3), 237-243 (1987)
   PUBMED   3327750
REFERENCE   2  (bases 1 to 7950)
  AUTHORS   Stillman,D.
  TITLE     Direct Submission
  JOURNAL   Submitted (19-MAY-1993) Stillman D.,
            e-mail:stillman@bioscience.utah.edu
COMMENT     Creating a Sequence File containing YCp50
            Based on Mark Rose's paper Gene 60, 237-243  (1987)
            
            1. Starting with pBR322, paste in 1.1 kb HindIII URA3 fragment into
            the AvaI site as follows: All overhangs chewed off, 10 G's added to
            nt 1428-1437 10 C's added to nt 2601-2610. [dG/dC tailing].  This
            is YIp5.
            
            2. CEN4 from PvuII to EcoRI was ligated to ARS1 EcoR1 to Hind III.
            Then 190 nt was deleted around EcoRI site [85 nt on either side.] I
            have deleted the BalI site; Rose left this intact, but were not
            sure.
            
            3. The CEN4-ARS1 fragment [PvuII - CEN4 - dead EcoRI - ARS1 -
            HindIII/klenowed] was put into the PvuII site of YIp5. Rose notes
            that the PvuII site was not regenerated.  To accomplish this, while
            retaining concordance with Rose's restriction site numbering, I
            changed CAGCTG to CAGGTG.
